# Which model server the benchmark agent talks to.
#
# Copy to .env in the repository root and edit. The agent CLI
# (agent/harness/agent.py) and the local lifecycle wrapper
# (dev/agent_lifecycle.py) both read it. An exported shell variable wins over
# this file, and a command-line flag wins over both, so .env only supplies what
# you have not set another way. .env is ignored by git; keep real keys there.
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works: the agent speaks that protocol and knows
# nothing else about the server. Uncomment one block.

# --- Self-hosted vLLM, port-forwarded by dev/model_server.sh (the default) ---
AGENT_MODEL=qwen3.8-27b
AGENT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8001/v1
AGENT_API_KEY=EMPTY

# --- Self-hosted vLLM reached in-cluster (agent Job, no port forward) ---
# AGENT_MODEL=qwen3.8-27b
# AGENT_BASE_URL=http://vllm-qwen38-service/v1
# AGENT_API_KEY=EMPTY

# --- Local Ollama ---
# AGENT_MODEL=qwen3:8b
# AGENT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# AGENT_API_KEY=ollama

# --- OpenAI ---
# AGENT_MODEL=gpt-4o
# AGENT_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# AGENT_API_KEY=sk-...

# --- Mistral (OpenAI-compatible endpoint) ---
# AGENT_MODEL=mistral-large-latest
# AGENT_BASE_URL=https://api.mistral.ai/v1
# AGENT_API_KEY=...

# Optional: bexhoma's result folder, otherwise taken from cluster.config.
# AGENT_RESULTS=/path/to/results
